\begin{proposition}[Euler numbers in semistable toric rank-two models]\label{cdp:st:C2c}
\StatementRecord{cdp:st:C2c}{proved}{Historical records: GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, 17 November 2026; Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic), effort high, 16 November 2026. Also checked in this writing by \CurrentChecker. The cone fan over the explicit unimodular triangles gives t=x1*x2*x3. The lattice shear acts by the displayed t-periods; logarithmic barycentric coordinates prove proper discontinuity and compact representatives, giving a proper analytic quotient with the stated product torus nearby. Its vertex and triangle counts give every positive even Euler number. Mumford section6 pp265-268 was opened with its complete-DVR hypotheses; the analytic quotient is established by the receiving proof's own maps}{the hypotheses, notation and definitions stated here; \cite[Section~6, especially (6.3)--(6.7)]{Mumford1972}}

Consider a rank-two Mumford model with smooth three-dimensional total space obtained from a unimodular periodic triangulation of $\R^2$, divided by a rank-two translation lattice acting freely on the total model. Let $V,E,F$ be the numbers of vertices, edges and triangles in the quotient triangulation. Its reduced central fibre has Euler number
\[
 e(S)=F=2V\in2\Z_{>0}.                                \tag{C.2}\label{cdp:eq:C.2}
\]
Every positive even number occurs in this class. A rank-one model assembled from $\PP^1$-bundles over elliptic curves with their boundary elliptic sections identified has Euler number zero.
\end{proposition}

